preConditionHook:
// GRIMES'S FIRST PULLBACK TRIGGER (G06-03): the line bounding the pullback is
// penetrated and price recovers straight back across it. The bounding line is
// mechanized as the pullback's SHIFTED WINDOW EXTREME (merge decision 7 and
// decision 20 -- the window extreme, never a drawn or projected line), so a
// LONG needs the PREVIOUS bar to have traded below the lowest low of the
// pullbackLookback bars ending TWO bars ago, while THIS bar closes back above
// that same level. The short mirrors on the highs.
//
// The level is read at offset 2, not 1, so the breaking bar's own low cannot
// define the level it is said to have broken.
//
// NOT StopRunReclaimReentry, whose level is a CONFIRMED SWING PIVOT and whose
// trigger is this bar taking out the PRIOR BAR's high by a tick -- a different
// level and a different bar. NOT DipBelowPriorLowCloseBackAbove, whose level is
// the single prior bar's low and whose dip and recovery are the SAME bar. NOT
// TrendLineBreak, which is the PROJECTED-line form (decision 20).
//
// KEPT WHOLE like a crossing: the break and the recovery are one event, and no
// pane-AND pairs them because every entry pane evaluates on the SAME bar -- the
// break is tested on bar 1 and the recovery on bar 0.
//
// The scan mirrors EasyLanguage's Extremes(), which Highest()/Lowest() call:
// seeded at the window's FIRST bar (offset 2 here, because the window is
// shifted by two), scanning the rest with a STRICT comparison so a tie keeps
// the earliest bar. Extremes is EL SOURCE, so its comparisons carry the
// relational tolerance and use el_lt / el_gt rather than raw < and >.
//
// SHIFT TEST: every comparison is a price against a price drawn from the same
// series, so the rule is invariant under a constant added to the whole series.
//
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope: the generator
// only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration is a redefinition
// when this rule is placed twice in one strategy. Every one is fully assigned
// each bar before it is read.
lvlLo = low[2];
lvlHi = high[2];
for (int i = 3; i <= (int)pullbackLookback + 1; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], lvlLo)) lvlLo = low[i];
    if (el_gt(high[i], lvlHi)) lvlHi = high[i];
}
